    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (70.69) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.32). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor and a weak SP_xERA of 4.97, overcoming his platoon disadvantage against Springs. Despite the SB threat from an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher, his spot in the three-hole makes him a foundational play. **Kyle Tucker** remains a premium asset despite a lower lineup position; his elite efficiency score is driven by a strong park factor and the ability to leverage his skill set against Valdez, F, whose xERA of 4.40 suggests vulnerability to our sluggers. **Drake Baldwin** (69.58) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) also provide significant value today, with **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s leadoff status against the beatable Adams, M providing a high floor for Runs and OBP contribution.\n\nStrategy today hinges on capitalizing on specific matchups, such as **Sam Antonacci** (63.20), whose leadoff opportunity against Matthews, R and strong platoon advantage make him a sneaky high-value play. While **Luis Robert Jr.** (58.94) faces an elite opposing pitcher, his score is bolstered by wind blowing out, providing a unique upside if he connects. The toughest decision involved leaving **Wade Meckler** (40.63) on the bench. While his leadoff profile and neutral park factors are serviceable, he lacked the explosive platoon or park-adjusted ceiling of our starting outfielders. We continue to monitor the IL status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson**, whose absences leave us lean, forcing heavy reliance on depth pieces like **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven SB and AVG categories.",
